# mutgap4_sys_iosfc_plane_extended_left_v1: A plane's extendedPixelsOnLeft reaches the IOSurface as kIOSurfacePlaneExtendedPixelsOnLeft: one-plane 16x8 BGRA surfaces (a good plane) with 8 extra columns on the left in a plane of 512 bytes (bytesPerRow 64) and in one of 768 bytes (bytesPerRow 96), then 0, v1 (plane byte 0x28) and v2 (plane +0x40), each mapped then tested; each status and data page is locked. Measured: the 512-byte plane with 8 left columns is refused (BadArgument), the 768-byte one maps (the test writes 768 bytes), and the plane with none maps.
